Model answer — the hardcoded endpoint <p>Flaws (any three):</p> <ul> <li>Functionally dead: the hardcoded <code>"positive"</code> is returned regardless of input — no model, no reading of <code>text</code></li> <li>No validation: empty/missing text isn't rejected — it silently returns garbage</li> <li>Wrong method: GET puts text in the URL — exposed in logs, truncated by length limits</li> <li>Silent failure: no error responses, so bad data propagates downstream</li> </ul> <p>Corrected design:</p> <pre><code>class SentimentRequest(BaseModel):
    text: str

@app.post("/sentiment")
def analyze(req: SentimentRequest):
    if not req.text.strip():
        raise HTTPException(400, "text cannot be empty")
    return {"sentiment": run_model(req.text)}
</code></pre> <p>POST (body payload, no limits, auth headers) · Pydantic schema at the boundary (fail fast, 400) · real inference · explicit errors, never silent.</p> Self-check <p>≥3 flaws ✓ · POST with reason ✓ · validation with 400 ✓ · real inference ✓</p>
